TITLE:: PathActionQMenu
summary:: A Button with a popup Menu for performing actions on file paths.
categories:: GUI>Views, Libraries>jostMlib
related:: jostMlib, Classes/ActionQSubMenu,  Classes/ActionQMenu, Classes/ActionMenu, Classes/PathActionMenu, Classes/Menu, Classes/MenuAction

DESCRIPTION::
An ActionQMenu, where string entries are interpreted as file/folder paths.

A folder works multi-level, listing subfolders.

You can still add \key->action associations,ActionQSubMenu,or a MenuAction just like in ActionQMenu.

Closes on click outside or on escape key.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Create an ActionMenu

ARGUMENT:: parent
The parent view.

ARGUMENT:: bounds
A Rect

ARGUMENT:: name
The Menu Button Title

ARGUMENT:: items
An Array of link::Classes/String::, link::Classes/Association:: (\key->function), link::Classes/MenuAction::, or link::Classes/ActionQSubMenu::.
Note:: items

A String is interpreted as file or folder paths (except if they start with "-");

A String ending in "/*" will iterated over the files in the directory on the top level.

If a String starts with "-", it creates a menu separator.

Use an Association to trigger the associated function (and globalAction).

Use a MenuAction to customize all aspects of the menu, and trigger the associated action (and globalAction).

Use a ActionQSubMenu to create a sub-menu.
::


ARGUMENT:: defaultAction
a default action, in case not action is specified.

ARGUMENT:: globalAction
a global action which is run for any item.

ARGUMENT:: useDefaultFont
if your item is a  , override its font with menu font.
defaults to true. If you want to completely customize MenuAction items, set it to false;


ARGUMENT:: lazyLoad
default: defaultLazyLoad. lazy load the submenus. False makes menu items more respnsive.

Caution: false can slow things down with large directories and subdirectories.

ARGUMENT:: showArrow
show a little down-tick arrow, defaults to true


returns::
an ActionQMenu

METHOD:: newMenuOnly
Create an ActionMenu without the trigger button, so you can attach the menu to link::Classes/MainMenu::

See code examples below.

